    <body>
      <div xml:id="gom-Isam24">
        <head xml:id="gom-Isam24-Hd1e98">Caput 24</head>
        <div xml:id="gom-Isam24-Dd1e100">
          <head xml:id="gom-Isam24-Hd1e102">Versus 4</head>
          <p xml:id="gom-Isam24-d1e104">
            <quote xml:id="gom-Isam24-Qd1e106" type="lemma" source="http://scta.info/resource/Isam24_4@11-12">Eratque ibi,</quote>
            etc.
            <ref xml:id="gom-Isam24-Rd1e109"><name xml:id="gom-Isam24-Nd1e110" ref="#RabanusMaurus">RAB.</name> ex Euch.</ref>
            <quote xml:id="gom-Isam24-Qd1e114"><seg type="qs">Rex ex improvisis exceptus insidiis</seg>, etc., usque ad <seg type="qs">ait Samuel: <quote xml:id="gom-Isam24-Qd1e120">Dirupit Dominus regnum Israel de manu tua.</quote></seg></quote>
          </p>
          <p xml:id="gom-Isam24-d1e123">
            <ref xml:id="gom-Isam24-Rd1e125" type="lemma" subtype="implied" target="http://scta.info/resource/Isam24_4@11-12"/>
            <ref xml:id="gom-Isam24-Rd1e127"><name xml:id="gom-Isam24-Nd1e128" ref="#GregoryGreat">GREG.</name>, Moral., tom. II.</ref>
            <quote xml:id="gom-Isam24-Qd1e132"><seg type="qs">Quid per Saul, nisi mali <pb ed="#P" n="0560D"/> rectores?</seg> etc., usque ad <seg type="qs">unde Moyses cum contra se et Aaron populum conqueri cognovisset, ait: <quote xml:id="gom-Isam24-Qd1e140" source="http://scta.info/resource/ex16_8@25-28">Nos enim quid sumus</quote>?</seg></quote>
          </p>
          <p xml:id="gom-Isam24-d1e145">
            <quote xml:id="gom-Isam24-Qd1e147" type="lemma" source="http://scta.info/resource/Isam24_4">Vivit,</quote>
            <!-- check: lemma not matched to verse text -->
            etc. Defectiva litterae Josephus supplet: qui erant cum eo redarguebant eum. Servabat enim inimicum qui volebat delere eum, et sedavit eos, dicens: <quote xml:id="gom-Isam24-Qd1e152">Vivit Dominus,</quote> etc.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </body>
